  "id": "controlled-processing",
  "term": "controlled processing",
  "definition": "Controlled processing is a conscious, deliberate form of thinking that is flexible but uses substantial mental resources. In social cognition, it is contrasted with more automatic processing, which is faster and less demanding but less flexible.",
